[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a situation where I want to first prove a hypothesis about an inductive type and then rewrite its index. The problem is that the original term is not equal to the new term since I have rewritten its index so I can't use the original hypothesis later.</p>\n<p>Here's a minimal working example with the same problem:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vec</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>how can I use h' for vec after rewriting?</p>",
        "id": 580643241,
        "sender_full_name": "Syed Shaazib Tanvir",
        "timestamp": 1774009054
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this is usually not something you want to do, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Vector.cast#doc\">docs#Vector.cast</a></p>",
        "id": 580644247,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774009373
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you can try <code>revert vec</code> followed by <code>rw [h]</code> and it will rewrite the hypothesis <code>h'</code> as well since you moved it into the goal</p>",
        "id": 580644341,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774009408
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks a lot, this worked.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Rewriting.20Index.20of.20an.20Inductive.20Type/near/580644247\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>this is usually not something you want to do, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Vector.cast#doc\">docs#Vector.cast</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I do think there's probably a simpler way but I  couldn't think of anything other than rewriting the index.<br>\nThe theorem I used it for can be found <a href=\"https://github.com/shaazib-tanvir/ContextFree/blob/8fd1092299c21464497d08e6b0a141aaded9b09a/ContextFree/ParseTree.lean#L194\">here</a>.<br>\nI had to prove the intermediate lemma</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_decreasing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">child_derives</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>in order to do strong induction and I also had to rewrite the index of <code>child_derives</code> to apply this lemma</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">ContextFreeGrammar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_append_derives'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u_1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u_1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContextFreeGrammar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NT</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">terminal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ws</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SizeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SizeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SizeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SizeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derives'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ws</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
